prompt Keep taking the next agent-doable Lindy-first crux; approve own design rounds; double-seat; send each increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates.
think r1 and r2 landed and sent — the fake net issues, taxes, and reserves stars under one sovereign hand. The exploration doc named r3 plainly: render a folded ledger to a format constel-ledger-v1 Bron record and parse it back byte-for-byte, the safe name and the sovereign key riding with it. Agent-doable, reaches no custody gate. This mirrors the harness's own r3 (constel_net_bron.rye), which travelled only a roster of numbers.
think The distinctive crux over the harness's r3: a ledger fact carries a signature. To travel and still fold, each fact needs kind·amount·star·signature, and the signer's key. Every admitted fact's signer IS the sovereign, so the sovereign key rides once as its own line and each reconstructed fact binds it as signer_pk. Then supply() re-folds through the real Mycelium law, which verifies every signature against that carried key — so a record whose sovereign line does not match its facts refuses IdentityRefused. The sovereignty is load-bearing in the bytes, not a note. That is r3's own crux, distinct from the harness's number-only roster.
think Ledger facts minted via issue/tax/reserve carry an empty body (mint_fact called with body ""), so the record need carry no body — asserted body_len==0 in from_ledger and in read_fact, so none is silently dropped. Star token renders the star name for reservations and a sentinel "-" for issue/tax (a real star name is never a lone dash). The reader is a purpose-built bounded flat-Bron reader over the tree's key value idiom, the hex helpers borrowed from council_sky_bron. Composed rungs one and two over public API only; both re-run GREEN at r3's door.
obs Landed pond/apps/constel_net_ledger_bron.rye + tools/constel_net_ledger_bron_witness.rish. One build red caught same-round: the tokens buffer was sized [4] but a fact line carries five tokens (fact·kind·amount·star·sig) — grew it to [5], GREEN. Selftest GREEN (8 cases): round-trip recovers safe name + sovereign key + supply 50 over three facts, re-render byte-for-byte identical (fixed point) · a swapped sovereign key refuses IdentityRefused on the fold (the sovereignty crux) · an @p-shaped net name refuses UnsafeName (the quarantine travels) · unknown field · bad header · missing net · missing sovereign · bad hex each refuse. Witness GREEN, re-runs r2 at its door; tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0.
obs Reaches no custody gate: the fold is a supply model, not a payment rail (gate #3); no real key/funds/network (gate #4); a ledger served over the wire reaches the serve gate. Sent as its own signed round on both remotes (origin + xykj61).
